{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"agent_message","text":"Built [**Killer Bee Night**](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-ultra.build-v2__20261106-030123__xe308f2/work/Killer-Bee-Night-Killer-Bees-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-030123.html). Open the HTML directly—no installation needed. **338/338 checks passed.**\n\n[Progress log](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-ultra.build-v2__20261106-030123__xe308f2/work/PROGRESS.md) · [Required interview](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-ultra.build-v2__20261106-030123__xe308f2/work/exit-interview.json)\n\n**Source Information**\n\n- Date: 2026-11-06 03:01:23. Source: *Killer Bees!* (1983). Plan: `PLAN.md`.\n- Genre/perspective: Action arcade, fixed overhead.\n- Tech: my-3D2dge 0.89.1, Hub SDK 1.4.0, JavaScript, Canvas, Web Audio and WebRTC.\n- Art/animation: Original procedural pixel gardens and insects; custom native Blob-derived rigs.\n- Audio: Original synthesized music, effects and gibberish voices; music defaults to 10%.\n- Online: Couch co-op, Hub shared-world/dedicated authority, manual WebRTC co-op.\n- Testing: Deterministic campaigns, three browser engines, controller/touch stand-ins, offline audio and real multiplayer harnesses.\n- Research: [Original manual](https://odyssey2.info/library/manuals/us_killerbees/Killer%20Bees%20(USA).pdf) and two creator interviews. Original sound/timing remains unknown.\n- Environment: Codex CLI, headless Linux. Model: OpenAI gpt-6.1-sol, ultra reasoning. Usage: **added on import**.\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n\n1. Eight distinct tested issues caught and fixed.\n2. Three were blocking or game-breaking.\n3. Most helpful: ordinary-command completion through all six encounters, followed by earned Hub victory.\n4. Least informative: syntax checks for judging combat and readability.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n\n1. Best features: native pixel rendering, procedural rigs, fixed stepping and menus.\n2. Initial mistakes involved canvas sizing, arena containment and half-key bindings.\n3. Largest custom system: deterministic combat and shared-world authority.\n4. Hardest integration: truthful geometry across portrait and TV layouts.\n5. Engine source changes: none; extended its existing systems.\n6. Suggested improvement: a fixed-arena fitting helper with reserved HUD/touch areas.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n\n1. Best part: specific combat and acceptance requirements.\n2. Confusion: “demo” versus the required complete campaign.\n3. Hardest part: integrating campaign balance with multiplayer and input lifecycles.\n4. Suggested change: distinguish essential gates from optional polish.\n\nPhysical-device testing, subjective listening and arbitrary internet/NAT connectivity remain unverified."}}
